From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:16:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd934x: derive EXT_CLK_DIV_RATIO from the MCLK rate

CLK_SYS_MCLK_PRG's EXT_CLK_DIV_RATIO field halves the external clock
before it reaches the codec's audio domain, and it is hardcoded to the
divide-by-two setting. Downstream picks it from the MCLK rate instead -
no division for 9.6 MHz, divide by two for 12.288 MHz - so on a 9.6 MHz
board the whole audio domain runs at half speed and every decimator
produces half the samples it was programmed for.

The defect is invisible to a pitch check, because the missing samples
come back as zero-stuffing rather than as a rate change: the stream is
still 48 kHz and still correctly pitched, it just carries 24 kHz of
content. What does show it is the spectrum. With a 3 kHz tone played at
the microphone of a Pixel 2 XL (a 9.6 MHz board), the capture carried an
image at 24 kHz - f with the same magnitude as the fundamental, the
signature of a 24 kHz stream zero-stuffed to 48 kHz. With the divider
picked from the rate every image drops to the noise floor and the raw
samples read as a continuous sinusoid, 16 samples per cycle at 3 kHz.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 include/linux/mfd/wcd934x/registers.h | 1 +
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c            | 8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/mfd/wcd934x/registers.h b/include/linux/mfd/wcd934x/registers.h
index 661e5be0cf1b..72cc85ed5f6e 100644
--- a/include/linux/mfd/wcd934x/registers.h
+++ b/include/linux/mfd/wcd934x/registers.h
@@ -203,6 +203,7 @@
 #define WCD934X_EXT_CLK_BUF_EN_MASK	BIT(7)
 #define WCD934X_EXT_CLK_BUF_EN		BIT(7)
 #define WCD934X_EXT_CLK_DIV_RATIO_MASK	GENMASK(5, 4)
+#define WCD934X_EXT_CLK_DIV_BY_1	0x00
 #define WCD934X_EXT_CLK_DIV_BY_2	0x10
 #define WCD934X_MCLK_SRC_MASK		BIT(1)
 #define WCD934X_MCLK_SRC_EXT_CLK	0
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
index 9aa451632fb4..85432623c6b2 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
@@ -1297,9 +1297,15 @@ static int wcd934x_enable_ana_bias_and_sysclk(struct wcd934x_codec *wcd)
 	regmap_update_bits(wcd->regmap, WCD934X_CLK_SYS_MCLK_PRG,
 			   WCD934X_EXT_CLK_BUF_EN_MASK,
 			   WCD934X_EXT_CLK_BUF_EN);
+	/*
+	 * The external clock divider halves MCLK before it reaches the audio
+	 * domain, so it must follow the rate the board actually feeds in:
+	 * 9.6 MHz is used as-is, 12.288 MHz is divided by two.
+	 */
 	regmap_update_bits(wcd->regmap, WCD934X_CLK_SYS_MCLK_PRG,
 			   WCD934X_EXT_CLK_DIV_RATIO_MASK,
-			   WCD934X_EXT_CLK_DIV_BY_2);
+			   wcd->rate == WCD934X_MCLK_CLK_9P6MHZ ?
+			   WCD934X_EXT_CLK_DIV_BY_1 : WCD934X_EXT_CLK_DIV_BY_2);
 	regmap_update_bits(wcd->regmap, WCD934X_CLK_SYS_MCLK_PRG,
 			   WCD934X_MCLK_SRC_MASK,
 			   WCD934X_MCLK_SRC_EXT_CLK);
